1
00:00:01,419 --> 00:00:02,253
Ito?

2
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,170
Ito.

3
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:06,507
Hot spring town.

4
00:00:07,091 --> 00:00:09,218
I'm so excited.

5
00:00:10,886 --> 00:00:11,929
Go, go!

6
00:00:12,596 --> 00:00:14,265
What's with the guys?

7
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,350
Yeah, the guys.

8
00:00:16,434 --> 00:00:18,269
They're going to gossip
and stuff, aren't they?

9
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:20,604
The way Yoko drives looks so cool.

10
00:00:20,688 --> 00:00:21,605
So cool.

11
00:00:22,106 --> 00:00:23,441
I want to take a mixed-gender bath.

12
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:24,483
I bet.

13
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,820
So naughty.

14
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:30,114
He said he wanted to take
a bath with the girls.

15
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:32,658
That would really get me excited.

16
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:35,369
Isn't this the place?

17
00:00:35,453 --> 00:00:36,954
What?

18
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,622
-This is it.
-There.

19
00:00:39,248 --> 00:00:41,208
It looks like a mansion.

20
00:00:41,292 --> 00:00:42,585
I'm so jealous.

21
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:44,670
We'd love to go, too.

22
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:47,339
It's a nice place.

23
00:00:48,007 --> 00:00:49,258
So warm.

24
00:00:58,350 --> 00:00:59,685
Is this allowed?

25
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:01,937
How nice.

26
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:06,525
When my X and I would visit
a hot spring, even if it came with a bath,

27
00:01:06,609 --> 00:01:08,152
she wouldn't get in with me.

28
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,070
We always went in separately.

29
00:01:10,154 --> 00:01:11,363
Separately?

30
00:01:12,198 --> 00:01:14,617
You didn't get mad?

31
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:17,077
I would get my fun later.

32
00:01:18,162 --> 00:01:19,371
How lame.

33
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,292
Table tennis?

34
00:01:25,461 --> 00:01:27,046
There's a letter.

35
00:01:28,297 --> 00:01:33,302
You will now hold a table tennis
tournament together.

36
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:39,016
The winner

37
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:42,770
will choose one person

38
00:01:42,853 --> 00:01:47,942
to spend the night with in a special room
with an open-air bath.

39
00:01:49,652 --> 00:01:51,153
And the next morning,

40
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:55,616
they will go on a special date
to watch the sun rise

41
00:01:55,699 --> 00:01:57,493
over the beautiful Pacific Ocean.

42
00:01:57,576 --> 00:01:58,994
What?

43
00:01:59,078 --> 00:02:00,246
Just one pair?

44
00:02:01,539 --> 00:02:02,706
Seriously?

45
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,041
But I want to stay in that room.

46
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:06,210
So the winner gets to choose.

47
00:02:06,544 --> 00:02:10,923
Draw from the bucket to determine
the matchups

48
00:02:11,006 --> 00:02:13,259
and follow the tournament bracket.

49
00:02:15,219 --> 00:02:16,345
Ready?

50
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:17,429
There.

51
00:02:17,513 --> 00:02:18,347
So good!

52
00:02:19,974 --> 00:02:21,267
Mao-chan wins.

53
00:02:22,268 --> 00:02:23,644
He's putting so much spin on it.

54
00:02:26,939 --> 00:02:27,815
Ready?

55
00:02:32,069 --> 00:02:33,445
Daichi, Mao.

56
00:02:33,529 --> 00:02:34,697
Daichi and Mao in the finals.

57
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,866
Daichi versus Mao?

58
00:02:36,949 --> 00:02:37,867
We got Daichi versus Mao.

59
00:02:37,950 --> 00:02:39,368
It's Daichi versus Mao.

60
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:43,622
I haven't really faced

61
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,791
my X properly yet.

62
00:02:45,875 --> 00:02:46,917
That's true.

63
00:02:47,251 --> 00:02:48,794
So I think I'll ask my X.

64
00:02:51,881 --> 00:02:52,840
Then win.

65
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:55,843
Seriously, win then.

66
00:02:57,177 --> 00:02:58,762
Nice shot.

67
00:02:58,846 --> 00:02:59,847
Nice shot!

68
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:06,103
Do you think Mao will ask Hikaru
if she wins?

69
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:07,313
Good question.

70
00:03:08,731 --> 00:03:10,608
Nice, nice.

71
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:11,567
I'm not sure.

72
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:12,610
This is a crucial match.

73
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:14,153
What's going through Ryo's mind?

74
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:15,070
This is fun.

75
00:03:17,865 --> 00:03:18,908
So close!

76
00:03:20,409 --> 00:03:22,202
Which means Dai-chan's at match point.

77
00:03:22,286 --> 00:03:23,662
He's at match point.

78
00:03:23,746 --> 00:03:24,872
Match point, Dai-chan.

79
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,878
That's game.

80
00:03:31,337 --> 00:03:33,088
That was a good battle.

81
00:03:34,006 --> 00:03:35,299
Thank you.

82
00:03:35,382 --> 00:03:36,425
Good game.

83
00:03:37,134 --> 00:03:39,678
I was ecstatic.

84
00:03:40,512 --> 00:03:43,349
I was really banking on this.

85
00:03:43,432 --> 00:03:44,850
So I'm super happy.

86
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,270
So we're going to find out here.

87
00:03:48,354 --> 00:03:50,189
Whoever he asks is his X.

88
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:53,525
Kaede-san, would you go with me?

89
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:02,910
Are you sure?

90
00:04:02,993 --> 00:04:04,620
Yes, please.

91
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:08,123
Of course, I have things
I want to ask her,

92
00:04:08,207 --> 00:04:11,418
and I want to get deep with her.

93
00:04:12,461 --> 00:04:14,296
Crap, I can't stop grinning.

94
00:04:15,297 --> 00:04:17,758
The fact that he can't stop grinning means

95
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:18,842
he totally loves her.

96
00:04:18,926 --> 00:04:21,595
I'm nervous. We'll be alone, right?

97
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,264
I'm nervous.

98
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:28,143
I want to know why they broke up so badly.

99
00:04:28,227 --> 00:04:30,312
I wonder what their relationship was like.

100
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:36,068
Wow.

101
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:36,986
Wow.

102
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:38,904
It's so roomy!

103
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:39,822
This is amazing.

104
00:04:39,905 --> 00:04:41,907
Maybe they broke up recently.

105
00:04:41,991 --> 00:04:43,534
Good point.

106
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:45,869
Like they broke up while still
liking each other.

107
00:04:45,953 --> 00:04:46,912
Wow.

108
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:48,080
This is quite the reward.

109
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:49,039
This is crazy.

110
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:51,000
The reward is too decadent.

111
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:53,961
I guess we're allowed such luxury.

112
00:04:54,044 --> 00:04:56,797
I never would've expected this.

113
00:04:57,172 --> 00:04:58,674
It's delicious.

114
00:04:58,841 --> 00:05:00,050
So cute.

115
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:01,510
This is a nice place.

116
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:02,845
The vibe is nice.

117
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:05,514
They're not awkward with each other
at all.

118
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:08,559
It's nice outside, too.

119
00:05:08,809 --> 00:05:10,894
This is way too amazing.

120
00:05:10,978 --> 00:05:12,896
It's magical.

121
00:05:16,275 --> 00:05:19,945
Back when we broke up,

122
00:05:21,155 --> 00:05:24,324
we talked a whole bunch and
came to an understanding,

123
00:05:26,410 --> 00:05:27,578
acting all mature.

124
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:33,333
I agreed because I thought it was better

125
00:05:34,043 --> 00:05:36,211
than never seeing you again.

126
00:05:36,754 --> 00:05:39,798
But I've always regretted it.

127
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:44,344
That's why I agreed to participate
in this hocance.

128
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,973
So it was Kaede who ended it
like I thought.

129
00:05:48,057 --> 00:05:49,933
I guess so.

130
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:53,312
Uncle still loves Kaede.

131
00:05:54,396 --> 00:05:56,482
So I wanted to face you again

132
00:05:57,691 --> 00:06:00,027
and talk again.

133
00:06:02,446 --> 00:06:06,241
I wanted to see you again,
and I wanted you to see me again, too.

134
00:06:06,325 --> 00:06:07,618
I wonder what happened.

135
00:06:10,913 --> 00:06:12,456
I see.

136
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:18,754
Can I ask you what your intention was

137
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:22,674
in inviting me to this hocance?

138
00:06:22,758 --> 00:06:24,468
-Intention?
-I mean.

139
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:25,761
There must be something, right?

140
00:06:26,637 --> 00:06:28,555
Right?

141
00:06:28,639 --> 00:06:32,643
I think you can see through this hocance

142
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:38,482
that I'm trying to get you
to fall in love with me again

143
00:06:40,317 --> 00:06:42,653
through my actions.

144
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:47,491
He's saying some cool things.

145
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:49,451
I can't see any flaws.

146
00:06:49,535 --> 00:06:51,328
Not at all at this point.

147
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:53,914
I see.

148
00:06:55,499 --> 00:06:56,792
I'm looking forward to it.

149
00:06:57,668 --> 00:06:59,044
Your face is close.

150
00:06:59,128 --> 00:07:00,546
You're making me nervous.

151
00:07:02,089 --> 00:07:02,923
I look forward to it.

152
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,216
Good.

153
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,517
So hot.

154
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:16,061
It's low-key just hot.

155
00:07:16,145 --> 00:07:17,729
How's the batter coming?

156
00:07:17,813 --> 00:07:20,107
Hey, Red and White!

157
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,276
Red and White!

158
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:23,819
They called them Red and White.

159
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:24,736
Red and White?

160
00:07:24,862 --> 00:07:26,405
Because of our shirts.

161
00:07:26,488 --> 00:07:27,906
What?

162
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:29,491
What now?

163
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:31,785
Is the batter heavy?

164
00:07:32,244 --> 00:07:33,203
I bet it is.

165
00:07:33,287 --> 00:07:34,830
I can't tell if it's heavy or not.

166
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:38,000
Come on now!

167
00:07:38,083 --> 00:07:39,376
You're asking the wrong person.

168
00:07:40,294 --> 00:07:42,045
Did you already have a choice
in mind if you won?

169
00:07:42,129 --> 00:07:43,005
Yeah.

170
00:07:43,088 --> 00:07:43,922
You did?

171
00:07:44,006 --> 00:07:44,923
Me too.

172
00:07:45,007 --> 00:07:46,091
I knew who I would pick.

173
00:07:46,175 --> 00:07:47,759
Wow.

174
00:07:47,843 --> 00:07:51,889
I had it down to two.

175
00:07:51,972 --> 00:07:54,266
Come on now!

176
00:07:54,349 --> 00:07:56,685
Why would he come out and say that?

177
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:59,271
I've never had an outburst on camera
like that before.

178
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:00,606
He drew it out of me.

179
00:08:00,689 --> 00:08:02,608
Wow, because there are only five choices.

180
00:08:02,691 --> 00:08:05,110
So two out of five.

181
00:08:05,194 --> 00:08:07,279
I was torn between the two.

182
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:08,989
At that moment.

183
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:10,407
I was like, which one?

184
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,450
I was, too.

185
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:14,661
The moment I heard the rule,
two people popped into my head.

186
00:08:14,745 --> 00:08:16,413
I see.

187
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,248
That was super skeezy.

188
00:08:18,332 --> 00:08:19,917
Skeezy.

189
00:08:21,168 --> 00:08:23,921
That he had two people to ask if he won.

190
00:08:24,004 --> 00:08:25,380
I totally got the ick.

191
00:08:33,347 --> 00:08:34,932
Wow.

192
00:08:35,015 --> 00:08:36,099
This is crazy.

193
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:37,309
This is amazing.

194
00:08:37,392 --> 00:08:38,977
They look so good together.

195
00:08:39,061 --> 00:08:40,687
They really are a good match.

196
00:08:40,771 --> 00:08:43,273
It's like we're walking towards the stars.

197
00:08:43,357 --> 00:08:44,441
Truly.

198
00:08:45,359 --> 00:08:47,945
The sunrise will be around there.

199
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:49,529
Over there?

200
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:52,199
It's beautiful.

201
00:08:52,282 --> 00:08:54,243
The stars are so pretty!

202
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:56,453
I'm glad we could come here together.

203
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:59,206
I'm so glad you won.

204
00:09:01,375 --> 00:09:03,377
They seem like they're already together.

205
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:04,753
Good point.

206
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:07,464
Maybe he meant getting the chance
to see this view with her.

207
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:09,967
There's something magical
about the sunrise.

208
00:09:10,926 --> 00:09:15,555
Like it's newly welcoming.

209
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:17,557
That's true.

210
00:09:17,641 --> 00:09:18,600
Like there's a meaning.

211
00:09:18,684 --> 00:09:20,018
I wonder why they broke up.

212
00:09:20,102 --> 00:09:21,311
I want to know, too.

213
00:09:47,838 --> 00:09:48,922
Long time no see.

214
00:09:49,715 --> 00:09:51,508
She seems happy.

215
00:09:53,885 --> 00:09:56,346
It's been a while.

216
00:09:56,972 --> 00:09:58,473
You lost weight.

217
00:10:00,851 --> 00:10:02,728
It's been a while.

218
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:05,147
You lost weight, didn't you?

219
00:10:06,398 --> 00:10:07,316
Healthy?

220
00:10:07,399 --> 00:10:09,443
My health is stable right now.

221
00:10:09,526 --> 00:10:11,278
Really? That's great.

222
00:10:12,112 --> 00:10:14,865
That was what
I was worried about the most.

223
00:10:16,366 --> 00:10:17,743
Are you really okay?

224
00:10:17,826 --> 00:10:18,952
I was so surprised.

225
00:10:19,411 --> 00:10:21,204
Suddenly hearing from you.

226
00:10:22,581 --> 00:10:24,124
I bet.

227
00:10:24,541 --> 00:10:26,168
I kept wondering why.

228
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:32,382
What did you think my intention was in
inviting you here?

229
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:34,051
I have no idea.

230
00:10:34,343 --> 00:10:37,471
No matter how much I think about it,

231
00:10:39,306 --> 00:10:42,059
it remains a mystery.

232
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:46,188
You probably already know,

233
00:10:47,189 --> 00:10:48,732
but I have experience

234
00:10:48,815 --> 00:10:52,611
with all sorts of people leaving me.

235
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:58,867
I really don't like that idea

236
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:01,411
of disappearing from someone's life.

237
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:03,538
It scares me.

238
00:11:04,373 --> 00:11:08,085
So if that's where this was headed,

239
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:12,422
when you asked me if we could
go back to being friends,

240
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:14,341
I thought I could go along with it

241
00:11:14,716 --> 00:11:17,260
if it meant not losing you.

242
00:11:17,344 --> 00:11:19,096
That was my thought process.

243
00:11:21,515 --> 00:11:23,183
And I agreed to it.

244
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:25,769
So.

245
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:31,858
I came here to see
if that was the right choice.

246
00:11:33,235 --> 00:11:35,320
That's the reason why
I decided to participate.

247
00:11:51,002 --> 00:11:55,549
I met Kaede in 2014.

248
00:11:55,841 --> 00:12:02,305
I remember thinking she was the most
beautiful woman I'd ever seen.

249
00:12:08,812 --> 00:12:13,859
And in 2018, my life hit rock bottom.

250
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:24,995
All the things I had built slowly over
the years started crumbling around me.

251
00:12:34,004 --> 00:12:37,257
I had lost my purpose and reason to live.

252
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:41,052
That's when I met Kaede.

253
00:12:47,476 --> 00:12:50,061
Simply put,

254
00:12:50,145 --> 00:12:52,105
I got divorced, faced litigation,

255
00:12:52,314 --> 00:12:54,774
and I lost my friends.

256
00:12:56,234 --> 00:12:59,738
That all happened in a six-month period.

257
00:13:00,197 --> 00:13:02,574
It was pure hell.

258
00:13:03,408 --> 00:13:08,288
I was at the level where I lost
my purpose for living.

259
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:17,005
Hearing he lost his purpose
and meaning to live,

260
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:28,433
I had no idea it was that bad.

261
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:34,898
And he was still so considerate of me
despite everything he was going through.

262
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:41,363
When I woke up in the middle of the night
from a nightmare,

263
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,907
I called Daichi-san on the phone
without hesitating,

264
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,618
and he would always pick up,
no matter how late it was.

265
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:49,788
He would gently ask what happened.

266
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:54,084
I remember how reassured I'd feel
after hearing his voice.

267
00:14:04,302 --> 00:14:08,640
It made me realize once again
how big of a heart he has.

268
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:14,729
I can't put it into words.

269
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:25,156
I end up branding myself a failure.

270
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,324
You do it yourself?

271
00:14:26,408 --> 00:14:27,659
Yes.

272
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:31,371
I label myself as no good.

273
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:32,998
A useless person.

274
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:34,708
A useless man.

275
00:14:34,791 --> 00:14:39,671
Like how could I possibly bring
anyone happiness?

276
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:46,177
But did that change after you
started dating your X?

277
00:14:46,261 --> 00:14:47,470
I changed.

278
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:52,267
I did. Which is why she's special.

279
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:55,687
I don't think it would've been possible
with anyone else.

280
00:14:56,146 --> 00:14:59,357
I thought the chances of meeting someone
like that were almost zero.

281
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:00,817
True.

282
00:15:02,277 --> 00:15:04,779
Which is why, Hikaru,

283
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:09,868
if someone whose forgiveness you need
to earn invited you to this hocance,

284
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:13,204
then I can't help but think,
go do your best, man.

285
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:22,297
I can't help but think,
"Don't be lame, man."

286
00:15:35,352 --> 00:15:37,646
Because Kaede was there for me
at that time,

287
00:15:37,729 --> 00:15:40,774
I was able to move forward with my life
once again.

288
00:15:46,029 --> 00:15:48,281
The time I spent with Kaede

289
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:52,577
was one of the most special
periods of my life.

290
00:15:55,747 --> 00:16:01,211
I want Kaede to find whatever happiness
she's looking for during this hocance.

291
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:20,814
After that, I was betrayed by
my so-called friend.

292
00:16:20,897 --> 00:16:24,067
He embezzled 10 million yen from me.

293
00:16:40,417 --> 00:16:44,379
She made me think, I'm allowed to live.

294
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:46,965
I'm allowed to live a normal life.

295
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:50,593
I was able to get that back for myself.

296
00:16:53,096 --> 00:16:55,890
She gets all the credit for it.
It was only her.

297
00:16:56,474 --> 00:17:01,104
Which is why in my mind,
I can never thank her enough.

298
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:06,192
I think it's that.

299
00:17:06,276 --> 00:17:07,485
Wow.

300
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:09,362
It's finally coming out.

301
00:17:09,446 --> 00:17:11,406
It just popped out of nowhere.

302
00:17:12,449 --> 00:17:14,200
That's how it comes out?

303
00:17:14,284 --> 00:17:15,618
So it comes out from below there?

304
00:17:15,702 --> 00:17:16,703
Wow.

305
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:19,789
Wow.

306
00:17:21,583 --> 00:17:23,001
Amazing.

307
00:17:29,924 --> 00:17:31,009
Wow.

308
00:17:31,092 --> 00:17:32,802
This is so moving.

309
00:17:32,886 --> 00:17:34,304
So fluorescent.

310
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,472
Yeah.

311
00:17:37,974 --> 00:17:39,601
What an amazing day.

312
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:40,935
Yeah.

313
00:17:41,019 --> 00:17:42,479
I'm glad we came.

314
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:44,564
It's dazzling.

315
00:17:44,647 --> 00:17:46,858
It really is.

316
00:17:47,984 --> 00:17:50,320
Her happiness

317
00:17:51,362 --> 00:17:53,406
is my greatest wish.

318
00:17:53,490 --> 00:17:57,619
And if I'm the one who can do that,
that would be the best.

319
00:18:11,049 --> 00:18:12,717
How many strawberries will you eat?

320
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,303
Let's hear it.

321
00:18:15,386 --> 00:18:16,805
300.

322
00:18:49,671 --> 00:18:51,422
Looking at the sun come up like this,

323
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:53,925
it's like, here's to a new beginning.

324
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:01,599
Thank you for coming with me.

325
00:19:01,683 --> 00:19:03,059
Thank you.

326
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:08,523
It was a really nice day.

327
00:19:08,606 --> 00:19:09,524
Yeah.

328
00:19:09,607 --> 00:19:11,067
I feel like we really connected.

329
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,151
Absolutely.

330
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:14,070
What an amazing reward.

331
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,196
It really was amazing.

332
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:23,872
Daichi-san would like to get back
together with Kaede-san.

333
00:19:23,955 --> 00:19:25,790
We don't know how Kaede-san
feels at this point.

334
00:19:25,874 --> 00:19:28,167
From what we saw, it looked
very promising.

335
00:19:28,251 --> 00:19:33,131
They seemed really good together,
so what happened

336
00:19:33,214 --> 00:19:37,093
to cause her to suggest
the two of them break up?

337
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:41,055
We don't know at this point.

338
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:45,810
What we know is

339
00:19:45,894 --> 00:19:48,938
she thought it would be better
if they went back to being friends.

340
00:19:49,022 --> 00:19:51,357
That was the reason she gave
for breaking up.

341
00:19:51,441 --> 00:19:52,275
But why?

342
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:53,192
Yeah, why?

343
00:19:53,276 --> 00:19:56,321
Plus, she was the one who initiated it,

344
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:59,699
but she was also the one
who invited him to Love Transit.

345
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:01,284
That's true.

346
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:05,455
Remember what Daichi said
while he was crying,

347
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:07,248
about deciding things about himself.

348
00:20:07,332 --> 00:20:10,001
Like someone like him
isn't allowed to be happy.

349
00:20:10,084 --> 00:20:11,461
Like self-denial?

350
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:12,462
Right.

351
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:15,590
If he's like, "I'm not allowed to
be happy, I'll just drag you down."

352
00:20:15,673 --> 00:20:19,552
And she's like, "Okay, then do you want
to go back to being friends?"

353
00:20:19,636 --> 00:20:22,221
Maybe she kept her distance out
of consideration for him.

354
00:20:22,305 --> 00:20:24,807
I see, like a separation.

355
00:20:25,016 --> 00:20:29,145
Okay, so summarizing everyone's
X situation,

356
00:20:29,437 --> 00:20:31,940
we can determine
that Ryo and Misato are Xs

357
00:20:32,023 --> 00:20:35,234
through the process of elimination.

358
00:20:35,318 --> 00:20:36,694
Right.

359
00:20:36,778 --> 00:20:39,113
They really haven't had a lot
of screentime so far.

360
00:20:46,037 --> 00:20:48,581
What are you making, Hika-chan?

361
00:20:49,207 --> 00:20:50,500
I'm just cutting a lemon.

362
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:55,004
Are you going to use that for something?

363
00:20:56,631 --> 00:20:58,508
Want to get some fresh air?

364
00:20:58,758 --> 00:21:00,051
Fresh air?

365
00:21:00,134 --> 00:21:01,010
Is it cold?

366
00:21:01,094 --> 00:21:02,971
No, I just want to bring my coffee.

367
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:03,930
Let's go.

368
00:21:04,013 --> 00:21:05,056
I want to.

369
00:21:05,473 --> 00:21:06,891
It's super cold.

370
00:21:06,975 --> 00:21:11,187
Do you want to go out together today?

371
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:12,230
Over there?

372
00:21:12,313 --> 00:21:13,648
Oh, you mean somewhere.

373
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:14,774
Sure.

374
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,987
I want to hear how you've been and stuff.

375
00:21:20,363 --> 00:21:24,867
Which means these two probably
weren't married to each other.

376
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,246
This is it.

377
00:21:28,329 --> 00:21:29,747
They look good together.

378
00:21:30,915 --> 00:21:32,709
They so look like they used to date.

379
00:21:34,252 --> 00:21:36,462
What? You're scaring me.

380
00:21:38,506 --> 00:21:40,008
What is that game? It looks fun.

381
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,261
I knew that was coming.

382
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:44,721
They look like they're having fun.

383
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:46,723
This looks to be the most like
everyday life.

384
00:21:47,932 --> 00:21:49,726
Cheers.

385
00:21:49,809 --> 00:21:50,768
Cheers.

386
00:21:53,896 --> 00:21:54,814
Hot…

387
00:21:54,897 --> 00:21:56,357
That looks hot.

388
00:21:56,941 --> 00:21:58,651
If we eat this, I won't be able
to eat dinner.

389
00:21:58,735 --> 00:21:59,902
For real?

390
00:22:00,111 --> 00:22:03,239
You eat like a bird.

391
00:22:03,489 --> 00:22:05,658
Were you always like that?

392
00:22:05,742 --> 00:22:06,993
Yeah.

393
00:22:07,410 --> 00:22:08,828
Can I ask you something?

394
00:22:08,911 --> 00:22:09,746
Go ahead.

395
00:22:09,829 --> 00:22:11,330
Why did you cry over the letter?

396
00:22:11,414 --> 00:22:13,082
Well,

397
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:16,794
it took me 20 years to understand
how I felt back then.

398
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:19,672
That long ago?

399
00:22:19,756 --> 00:22:21,758
So probably when they
were in college or something.

400
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:23,217
It was heavy.

401
00:22:23,301 --> 00:22:25,303
I think that's why I cried.

402
00:22:27,263 --> 00:22:30,600
I met Misato-san when we both
worked at the same part-time job.

403
00:22:30,683 --> 00:22:33,478
She looked very stylish, and was
so easy-going.

404
00:22:33,644 --> 00:22:36,981
Of all the people from my past,
I had the strongest feelings for her.

405
00:22:39,192 --> 00:22:44,655
What I remember most is when I was
hospitalized with a fever.

406
00:22:44,739 --> 00:22:48,242
I sensed that she visited me every day
before her shift

407
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:52,288
In my half-conscious state,

408
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:57,460
I remember falling for her
all over again at the time.

409
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:02,924
I wrote in my letter that you were
the woman I felt the strongest for.

410
00:23:03,007 --> 00:23:05,093
You were the one I was obsessed
with the most.

411
00:23:05,343 --> 00:23:07,678
That was true.

412
00:23:09,013 --> 00:23:10,306
Back then,

413
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:13,976
I was too young and embarrassed
to tell you.

414
00:23:14,852 --> 00:23:18,356
If you had told me

415
00:23:19,607 --> 00:23:21,359
something like that then.

416
00:23:22,026 --> 00:23:23,277
They were young.

417
00:23:23,361 --> 00:23:24,362
So they were too young.

418
00:23:24,487 --> 00:23:26,781
It might have turned out different.

419
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:31,369
Having grown older,

420
00:23:32,245 --> 00:23:34,497
he feels gentler.

421
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:40,837
He's way nicer than he was back then.

422
00:23:41,671 --> 00:23:45,508
So it was really novel.
I had a lot of fun.

423
00:23:46,175 --> 00:23:47,260
We're back.

424
00:23:48,970 --> 00:23:50,763
We're doing offal stew today.

425
00:23:50,847 --> 00:23:52,473
Is Kanako originally from Fukuoka?

426
00:23:54,016 --> 00:23:55,518
You're cute.

427
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:57,103
Offal stew suits you.

428
00:23:57,186 --> 00:23:58,146
I hope it's good.

429
00:23:58,229 --> 00:23:59,230
It's the taste of home.

430
00:23:59,313 --> 00:24:01,232
Do you say "sui touyo"
in the Hakata dialect?

431
00:24:01,315 --> 00:24:04,110
You mean like "like?" Maybe "sukicchan."

432
00:24:04,193 --> 00:24:05,361
Sukicchan?

433
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:07,238
I totally "sukicchan" this.

434
00:24:07,321 --> 00:24:09,407
So you say "sukicchan."

435
00:24:09,490 --> 00:24:11,159
Or "yo suiken."

436
00:24:11,242 --> 00:24:12,451
That's so cute.

437
00:24:12,535 --> 00:24:14,579
Can you use that for people too?

438
00:24:14,662 --> 00:24:15,955
Yeah.

439
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:18,583
So if I liked Hiro-san,

440
00:24:21,294 --> 00:24:24,422
it'd be like "I sukicchan you.
Would you go out with me?"

441
00:24:24,505 --> 00:24:25,923
That's cute.

442
00:24:26,007 --> 00:24:27,717
My heart just skipped a beat.

443
00:24:27,884 --> 00:24:30,261
Wait, I just confessed my love!

444
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:32,930
I arranged the food so neatly,
but nobody took pictures.

445
00:24:33,014 --> 00:24:33,848
That's true.

446
00:24:33,931 --> 00:24:35,016
Nobody took a picture.

447
00:24:35,099 --> 00:24:36,392
So I took it myself.

448
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:37,435
You did?

449
00:24:38,186 --> 00:24:41,105
You really are a Hakata woman.

450
00:24:41,564 --> 00:24:42,565
It's coming along.

451
00:24:42,648 --> 00:24:44,108
Why did you take a picture?

452
00:24:45,443 --> 00:24:48,196
I thought we would take a picture
after it was done.

453
00:24:48,279 --> 00:24:50,364
True.

454
00:24:50,448 --> 00:24:51,991
But that's an option too.

455
00:24:52,074 --> 00:24:52,992
I don't know.

456
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:55,244
It's fine.

457
00:24:55,661 --> 00:24:57,580
I thought we'd take it after it's done.

458
00:24:57,663 --> 00:24:59,165
Forget it.

459
00:24:59,457 --> 00:25:00,666
We'll take a picture after too!

460
00:25:00,750 --> 00:25:01,792
Yeah.

461
00:25:07,298 --> 00:25:09,217
I like Satoshi.

462
00:25:09,300 --> 00:25:12,470
Yeah, he never lies.

463
00:25:17,683 --> 00:25:18,976
What a great view.

464
00:25:19,060 --> 00:25:21,854
It makes me want to make out.

465
00:25:23,773 --> 00:25:27,276
What drew you to your X?

466
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:29,070
To X?

467
00:25:30,321 --> 00:25:31,864
Everything.

468
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:34,659
While she's beautiful,

469
00:25:34,742 --> 00:25:37,828
she's even more beautiful on the inside.

470
00:25:37,912 --> 00:25:40,039
You know?

471
00:25:40,122 --> 00:25:45,962
But I like everything else too.

472
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:49,966
So in my case,

473
00:25:50,299 --> 00:25:53,302
my X is someone I was with
a super long time ago.

474
00:25:54,262 --> 00:25:59,392
I thought I liked the unchanged
version of her.

475
00:25:59,642 --> 00:26:00,893
Right.

476
00:26:00,977 --> 00:26:03,938
But you know, people change
with the times,

477
00:26:04,021 --> 00:26:07,024
as they go through different experiences.

478
00:26:07,358 --> 00:26:09,735
But she hasn't changed at all.

479
00:26:09,986 --> 00:26:12,780
She's exactly the same as she was

480
00:26:12,863 --> 00:26:16,284
when I was super into her.

481
00:26:17,994 --> 00:26:19,787
She hasn't changed a bit.

482
00:26:20,329 --> 00:26:22,540
Like how are you the same!

483
00:26:23,708 --> 00:26:25,793
I was really happy about that.

484
00:26:25,876 --> 00:26:27,503
That she didn't change in a weird way.

485
00:26:27,753 --> 00:26:32,300
I'm glad she hasn't changed.

486
00:26:33,134 --> 00:26:37,888
I was so into her.

487
00:26:37,972 --> 00:26:40,308
I loved her so much.

488
00:26:40,558 --> 00:26:41,934
That's cool.

489
00:26:42,018 --> 00:26:43,894
So I wonder why they broke up.

490
00:26:43,978 --> 00:26:45,021
True.

491
00:26:45,104 --> 00:26:46,480
What's the reason?

492
00:26:46,731 --> 00:26:48,691
I wanted to show her off.

493
00:26:48,774 --> 00:26:50,401
That's so cool.

494
00:26:50,526 --> 00:26:52,361
Yeah?

495
00:26:52,445 --> 00:26:53,904
I think so.

496
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:57,992
But also, heads up,

497
00:26:58,075 --> 00:27:01,871
if it turns out that I like your X,

498
00:27:01,954 --> 00:27:03,622
I'm going for it.

499
00:27:05,041 --> 00:27:07,168
What's this?

500
00:27:07,918 --> 00:27:10,296
Right now,

501
00:27:11,589 --> 00:27:13,966
I'm 60 percent into Mao-chan.

502
00:27:14,050 --> 00:27:15,760
Seriously?

503
00:27:15,843 --> 00:27:16,844
Really?

504
00:27:16,927 --> 00:27:18,179
No way.

505
00:27:18,262 --> 00:27:20,806
Wait, now I remember
he was part of TeamMao.

506
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:23,434
Now that you mention it.

507
00:27:24,226 --> 00:27:29,857
I picked Mao-chan at first
just from her appearance.

508
00:27:30,441 --> 00:27:31,942
I mean,

509
00:27:33,778 --> 00:27:36,781
it's hard to put into words,

510
00:27:37,114 --> 00:27:40,451
but something gave me pause.

511
00:27:42,912 --> 00:27:44,038
Ready?

512
00:27:44,121 --> 00:27:45,206
Is it okay?

513
00:27:46,832 --> 00:27:48,709
All right. Crap.

514
00:27:48,793 --> 00:27:50,378
It smells good.

515
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:52,296
You washed it for us?

516
00:27:52,630 --> 00:27:54,006
Yeah.

517
00:27:54,256 --> 00:27:56,717
I'm prepared to go to battle.

518
00:28:04,892 --> 00:28:06,060
Wow.

519
00:28:06,143 --> 00:28:07,812
We haven't had this kind of…

520
00:28:07,895 --> 00:28:09,522
Now that's reality TV!

521
00:28:09,605 --> 00:28:10,981
Yeah, you're right.

522
00:28:11,065 --> 00:28:13,359
Ryo, who hasn't really made any moves
so far,

523
00:28:13,442 --> 00:28:17,488
turns out to be ten times more manly
than we imagined.

524
00:28:17,571 --> 00:28:18,906
I'm so curious.

525
00:28:18,989 --> 00:28:21,617
Did you see Hikaru do a double-take?

526
00:28:22,576 --> 00:28:24,161
Like "What?"

527
00:28:24,245 --> 00:28:25,413
I can't blame him.

528
00:28:25,496 --> 00:28:26,956
He was like this at the end.

529
00:28:27,039 --> 00:28:28,541
Like he said his piece.

530
00:28:28,624 --> 00:28:29,750
Like this?

531
00:28:30,084 --> 00:28:31,919
Now, how does Misato-san feel?

532
00:28:32,044 --> 00:28:33,170
Right.

533
00:28:33,254 --> 00:28:39,510
She reunited with Ryo-chan here
at the hocance,

534
00:28:39,593 --> 00:28:41,053
but is she interested in someone else?

535
00:28:41,137 --> 00:28:42,555
Right.

536
00:28:42,638 --> 00:28:44,890
Or does she want to try again
with Ryo-san?

537
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:51,272
Do we have spices?

538
00:28:51,355 --> 00:28:53,482
Good morning.

539
00:28:55,109 --> 00:28:57,778
The two rivals are sitting next
to each other.

540
00:28:57,862 --> 00:29:00,114
Good morning.

541
00:29:00,197 --> 00:29:02,450
Good morning. You look cute.

542
00:29:07,538 --> 00:29:08,873
Hey.

543
00:29:12,168 --> 00:29:13,544
What's up?

544
00:29:15,296 --> 00:29:17,256
Ryo has invited Mao.

545
00:29:18,007 --> 00:29:20,342
So today, well…

546
00:29:20,426 --> 00:29:23,637
we're going to go eat Cuban food.

547
00:29:23,721 --> 00:29:24,889
What?

548
00:29:24,972 --> 00:29:26,056
We're going to get Cuban food.

549
00:29:26,140 --> 00:29:27,349
What is that like?

550
00:29:27,433 --> 00:29:28,934
What?

551
00:29:29,018 --> 00:29:30,519
So what do you think?

552
00:29:30,603 --> 00:29:31,645
Okay, sure.

553
00:29:31,729 --> 00:29:33,063
Do we have the same hairstyle?

554
00:29:33,147 --> 00:29:34,607
I did it just now on purpose to match.

555
00:29:34,690 --> 00:29:36,108
You did?

556
