You look great.

831
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:54,387
He came back.

832
00:41:54,471 --> 00:41:55,931
Mao.

833
00:41:57,307 --> 00:42:00,018
That's not me.

834
00:42:00,268 --> 00:42:01,561
I'm embarrassed.

835
00:42:01,645 --> 00:42:03,313
My original look was facial hair
with glasses.

836
00:42:04,314 --> 00:42:06,191
What? Again?

837
00:42:07,359 --> 00:42:08,360
It's super cold.

838
00:42:08,443 --> 00:42:09,653
Then I don't want to.

839
00:42:09,736 --> 00:42:11,112
Hikaru-chan will do it, I bet.

840
00:42:13,156 --> 00:42:15,784
Yikes, it's super cold. What's up?
What happened?

841
00:42:15,867 --> 00:42:18,245
Wow, it really is cold.

842
00:42:19,829 --> 00:42:20,914
What?

843
00:42:26,378 --> 00:42:28,922
I was wondering if we could go out
on a date tomorrow.

844
00:42:29,464 --> 00:42:33,134
I've been meaning to talk to you
at the right time.

845
00:42:34,135 --> 00:42:39,557
And also ask you out on a date.

846
00:42:40,934 --> 00:42:44,271
So I would be grateful if you could
give me your time tomorrow.

847
00:42:44,896 --> 00:42:47,148
Please.

848
00:42:50,235 --> 00:42:54,281
The first thought I had was that
this was coming too late.

849
00:42:54,364 --> 00:42:59,494
But I was happy
that he finally took action.

850
00:42:59,661 --> 00:43:01,204
Also,

851
00:43:01,413 --> 00:43:07,377
I do plan on just enjoying
going out together.

852
00:43:07,669 --> 00:43:12,507
I've been wanting to go out with X
this whole time,

853
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:17,887
and I do have something
I want to tell her,

854
00:43:17,971 --> 00:43:21,349
but more than that, I just wanted
to spend time with her.

855
00:43:22,142 --> 00:43:24,227
He's lacking the sense of urgency.

856
00:43:24,311 --> 00:43:26,604
It's been a while since we drove together.

857
00:43:26,688 --> 00:43:28,440
The weather is so nice today.

858
00:43:28,523 --> 00:43:30,317
Yeah,

859
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:34,529
I wanted it to be a sunny day.

860
00:43:34,821 --> 00:43:38,366
Right, I remember you talking
about the weather.

861
00:43:38,450 --> 00:43:40,744
Right.

862
00:43:40,827 --> 00:43:43,246
I had a feeling you were talking about me.

863
00:43:43,788 --> 00:43:47,792
They do look like a married couple
when they're next to each other like this.

864
00:43:47,876 --> 00:43:48,877
That they're former spouses.

865
00:43:48,960 --> 00:43:50,420
Now that you mention it.

866
00:43:50,503 --> 00:43:52,172
What do we take a picture of first?

867
00:43:52,255 --> 00:43:53,465
Radishes!

868
00:43:53,548 --> 00:43:55,133
Let's go with radishes.

869
00:43:55,216 --> 00:43:58,386
Isn't that cute? I love them.

870
00:43:59,387 --> 00:44:01,473
It's like you're holding a strawberry.

871
00:44:01,848 --> 00:44:03,058
Even though it's a radish.

872
00:44:03,933 --> 00:44:05,810
I don't know how to respond to that.

873
00:44:06,102 --> 00:44:07,562
Here, let me have it.

874
00:44:07,979 --> 00:44:11,066
They seem to get along when they're
doing stuff like this.

875
00:44:11,149 --> 00:44:12,817
Isn't that so pretty?

876
00:44:12,901 --> 00:44:15,737
Yeah, let me see the bottom.

877
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:17,447
Wow, that's amazing.

878
00:44:18,281 --> 00:44:19,199
I dropped dirt on you.

879
00:44:20,909 --> 00:44:22,327
You did that on purpose.

880
00:44:22,410 --> 00:44:24,704
All you do is harass me and ruin my life.

881
00:44:24,913 --> 00:44:26,039
Hold on.

882
00:44:26,122 --> 00:44:27,082
She went pretty hard there.

883
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:30,377
I just got a little dirt on you,
and you bring up ruining your life?

884
00:44:38,718 --> 00:44:39,677
So good.

885
00:44:39,886 --> 00:44:40,804
Enjoy.

886
00:44:40,887 --> 00:44:42,222
Sorry, I already took the picture.

887
00:44:42,305 --> 00:44:43,973
I already took the picture.

888
00:44:44,557 --> 00:44:48,561
Somehow, there really is this mysterious
way that Xs

889
00:44:48,645 --> 00:44:49,896
just kind of click together.

890
00:44:49,979 --> 00:44:51,106
For sure.

891
00:44:51,398 --> 00:44:56,027
It had been a while, so it all
felt extremely nostalgic.

892
00:44:56,111 --> 00:44:59,572
And of course, I felt very happy.

893
00:44:59,781 --> 00:45:02,617
Our kids were really little at the time,

894
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:04,994
so it's probably been 10 years
since our last date.

895
00:45:05,078 --> 00:45:08,373
It felt so strange that we were
instantly able

896
00:45:08,456 --> 00:45:11,835
to go back to that time.

897
00:45:12,460 --> 00:45:14,462
Done.

898
00:45:14,546 --> 00:45:16,464
Let's dig in.

899
00:45:16,548 --> 00:45:19,134
Let's start with the salad. Thanks.

900
00:45:19,217 --> 00:45:20,135
No worries.

901
00:45:20,927 --> 00:45:21,845
Okay.

902
00:45:21,928 --> 00:45:24,764
That's yummy.

903
00:45:26,391 --> 00:45:29,978
You know how you don't talk while you eat?

904
00:45:30,270 --> 00:45:31,855
Basically.

905
00:45:33,481 --> 00:45:38,319
So if we had an hour to talk,
I wonder what we'd talk about.

906
00:45:41,948 --> 00:45:45,034
What's been on my mind this whole time…

907
00:45:46,995 --> 00:45:49,914
After doing the same thing
over and over…

908
00:45:50,165 --> 00:45:54,419
Despite feeling like
we were finally finished

909
00:45:54,502 --> 00:45:58,798
after the last thing I did,

910
00:45:59,466 --> 00:46:02,552
why did you still invite me
to this hocance?

911
00:46:03,553 --> 00:46:06,890
I've been curious about that.

912
00:46:10,935 --> 00:46:13,021
I calmed down.

913
00:46:14,022 --> 00:46:18,234
When I said we should split,
I was so worked up and angry.

914
00:46:20,528 --> 00:46:22,280
So,

915
00:46:22,906 --> 00:46:25,992
I probably said some hurtful things.

916
00:46:26,075 --> 00:46:28,536
So, you know,

917
00:46:29,454 --> 00:46:33,249
you did do some

918
00:46:34,417 --> 00:46:36,628
awful things to me,

919
00:46:36,711 --> 00:46:40,381
but the words I used regarding that

920
00:46:41,132 --> 00:46:42,926
may have been hurtful.

921
00:46:44,427 --> 00:46:48,223
So part of me feels bad about my actions
and words

922
00:46:48,306 --> 00:46:51,142
in response to what you did.

923
00:46:52,018 --> 00:46:57,190
I mean, we kept in contact to discuss
the kids and money.

924
00:46:58,900 --> 00:47:02,487
And we're probably going to stay
in touch for the foreseeable future

925
00:47:02,570 --> 00:47:05,281
for the kids and the financial matters

926
00:47:06,115 --> 00:47:10,787
as far as I can tell.

927
00:47:11,120 --> 00:47:14,874
So I wanted us to meet face to face
and talk about that

928
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:17,961
since we hadn't seen each other
in a while.

929
00:47:19,754 --> 00:47:23,091
That's the number one reason.

930
00:47:24,592 --> 00:47:26,844
So that means she does have some feelings.

931
00:47:26,928 --> 00:47:29,222
Or she wouldn't want to meet with him.

932
00:47:29,556 --> 00:47:30,848
For me,

933
00:47:31,808 --> 00:47:34,769
I suck at communicating.

934
00:47:35,937 --> 00:47:39,023
And sometimes I feel like
I've already said things to you

935
00:47:42,944 --> 00:47:45,446
because I'm doing so much thinking
inside my own head.

936
00:47:47,657 --> 00:47:50,159
Like how I constantly tell you,
"I already told you that."

937
00:47:50,243 --> 00:47:51,703
Right.

938
00:47:53,580 --> 00:47:56,207
So

939
00:47:57,208 --> 00:47:59,919
when things start feeling tedious to me,

940
00:48:00,003 --> 00:48:02,880
I tend to get reckless like I don't
even care what happens.

941
00:48:04,591 --> 00:48:05,550
Right.

942
00:48:07,010 --> 00:48:08,261
But

943
00:48:08,344 --> 00:48:12,640
I do think I shouldn't
be like that with you.

944
00:48:14,684 --> 00:48:18,271
Since you're important,
I know I need to face you properly.

945
00:48:18,354 --> 00:48:19,272
Yeah.

946
00:48:23,151 --> 00:48:27,280
When Ryo-chin asked me what I liked
about my X,

947
00:48:28,031 --> 00:48:30,491
and it might be a cliché,

948
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:32,118
but I told him I loved everything.

949
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:37,874
There's not a part of her I hate.

950
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:41,336
In that sense,

951
00:48:41,753 --> 00:48:44,297
you're already family.

952
00:48:44,756 --> 00:48:47,675
Even when people ask me,
"Do you love Hikaru-san?"

953
00:48:47,759 --> 00:48:50,553
Or "Do you love your X?"

954
00:48:50,637 --> 00:48:52,805
I'm like, "What is love?"

955
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:55,350
It's probably the same with you.

956
00:48:55,433 --> 00:48:56,976
I've always loved you.

957
00:48:58,144 --> 00:49:02,565
I probably told you even before
we split up,

958
00:49:03,858 --> 00:49:05,693
but I loved you more
than when we first met.

959
00:49:05,860 --> 00:49:08,446
Right, you did say that.

960
00:49:09,072 --> 00:49:11,991
You tell me you're always updating it.

961
00:49:14,452 --> 00:49:16,621
So that's how it is for me.

962
00:49:18,206 --> 00:49:22,919
I'd fall in love with you more each day

963
00:49:23,419 --> 00:49:24,921
if we were together.

964
00:49:25,004 --> 00:49:25,922
That's amazing.

965
00:49:28,174 --> 00:49:29,342
You're about to cry.

966
00:49:33,680 --> 00:49:36,808
Yeah, that's how it is for me.

967
00:49:37,725 --> 00:49:41,396
Right, you've always been saying that.

968
00:49:42,522 --> 00:49:44,232
You've kept saying that, but…

969
00:49:45,858 --> 00:49:48,736
If we end up together again,

970
00:49:50,738 --> 00:49:52,323
I'd…

971
00:49:57,245 --> 00:49:58,496
Yeah.

972
00:50:01,332 --> 00:50:04,419
I would love to fall in love with you more
each day.

973
00:50:18,015 --> 00:50:22,228
He's terrible at expressing his feelings.

974
00:50:22,395 --> 00:50:26,399
He hardly ever says those kinds of things
to my face.

975
00:50:27,191 --> 00:50:32,238
That's why I think what he conveyed
really came across.

976
00:50:32,572 --> 00:50:35,742
Do we get back together or not?

977
00:50:35,825 --> 00:50:39,662
If I only had the two choices,
I'd still be leaning towards not,

978
00:50:40,329 --> 00:50:43,416
but now I'm willing to think about it.

979
00:50:44,041 --> 00:50:48,296
The conversation we had
was able to sway me.

980
00:50:48,588 --> 00:50:52,133
I also have to factor
in our kids' feelings.

981
00:50:52,216 --> 00:50:55,052
I'm sure they'd prefer having
their dad around,

982
00:50:55,344 --> 00:50:59,849
and I think the kids are certainly
missing him to a certain degree.

983
00:50:59,932 --> 00:51:04,061
I believe that a father's presence
is big during critical moments.

984
00:51:04,520 --> 00:51:07,523
So part of me would like him around.

985
00:51:08,733 --> 00:51:12,195
I do think she's a wonderful woman,

986
00:51:12,278 --> 00:51:15,531
who treats everyone the same.

987
00:51:17,366 --> 00:51:20,203
She's just a wonderful woman.

988
00:51:20,286 --> 00:51:25,082
That was time well spent in my opinion.

989
00:51:30,505 --> 00:51:33,508
Well, it's just that…

990
00:51:35,176 --> 00:51:38,262
I've always wanted to go overseas
and give that venture a go.

991
00:51:38,346 --> 00:51:41,766
Or try to get a Michelin star.

992
00:51:43,935 --> 00:51:44,811
I see.

993
00:51:44,894 --> 00:51:46,145
He's got a big dream.

994
00:51:46,229 --> 00:51:47,688
I see.

995
00:51:47,772 --> 00:51:50,691
I haven't abandoned that.

996
00:51:50,942 --> 00:51:52,944
I don't think it's too late for me yet.

997
00:51:53,027 --> 00:51:54,987
He has a dream.

998
00:51:55,530 --> 00:51:59,951
It's still something that I'm always
thinking about in the back of my mind.

999
00:52:02,370 --> 00:52:04,872
He'd like to get back together with her,

1000
00:52:04,956 --> 00:52:08,835
but it doesn't seem like he's thinking
about living with her.

1001
00:52:08,918 --> 00:52:13,172
Maybe he feels having a home he can
return to gives him the courage to leave.

1002
00:52:13,589 --> 00:52:15,341
Like a fisherman?

1003
00:52:15,424 --> 00:52:19,136
Like he wants her to wait with the kids
for him or something.

1004
00:52:19,220 --> 00:52:23,349
I understand how men have dreams
they want to take a shot at…

1005
00:52:23,432 --> 00:52:28,312
Which is why he has to tell her
these things right now.

1006
00:52:28,396 --> 00:52:30,481
Or he'll become a liar again.

1007
00:52:30,565 --> 00:52:35,027
This is the difficult part
of Love Transit 35+.

1008
00:52:35,111 --> 00:52:37,029
Some things you can't get through
on feelings alone.

1009
00:52:37,113 --> 00:52:39,073
People have things going on
in their lives.

1010
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:41,742
Another difference with 35+ is that

1011
00:52:41,826 --> 00:52:44,453
in the living room,
they're just regular old men.

1012
00:52:45,705 --> 00:52:47,206
It's reassuring.

1013
00:52:47,290 --> 00:52:50,293
According to Misato, the reason
she broke up with Ryo-san

1014
00:52:51,085 --> 00:52:53,754
was his emotional abuse.

1015
00:52:53,838 --> 00:52:55,756
That was shocking.

1016
00:52:55,882 --> 00:52:58,759
Meaning from Misato-san's point of view.

1017
00:52:58,843 --> 00:53:02,388
We still haven't heard
Ryo-san's side of things

1018
00:53:02,555 --> 00:53:04,473
regarding their break-up.

1019
00:53:04,557 --> 00:53:07,476
I'm curious to find out how it seemed
from his end.

1020
00:53:08,019 --> 00:53:09,687
Shall we go for the next one?

1021
00:53:09,770 --> 00:53:10,855
Yes, let's do it.

1022
00:53:12,857 --> 00:53:15,568
Words of confession.

1023
00:53:15,860 --> 00:53:16,944
From our X?

1024
00:53:17,778 --> 00:53:20,323
We don't know if you were the one
saying it or receiving it.

1025
00:53:20,406 --> 00:53:23,284
It would be nice if we could hear
both as a set.

1026
00:53:23,367 --> 00:53:25,453
Everyone's trying to remember
what they were.

1027
00:53:25,536 --> 00:53:27,622
We're all digging through our memory.

1028
00:53:27,705 --> 00:53:28,915
I don't remember.

1029
00:53:28,998 --> 00:53:32,460
I can recite the whole thing
start to finish perfectly.

1030
00:53:32,543 --> 00:53:33,669
Really?

1031
00:53:33,753 --> 00:53:34,712
Wow.

1032
00:53:34,795 --> 00:53:35,922
Right in front of her.

1033
00:53:36,005 --> 00:53:37,173
Please share then.

1034
00:53:37,423 --> 00:53:38,841
We were in bed.

1035
00:53:38,925 --> 00:53:40,051
Oh, my.

1036
00:53:40,134 --> 00:53:41,928
What do you mean? For real?

1037
00:53:42,011 --> 00:53:46,515
That means you've already spent
the night together.

1038
00:53:46,766 --> 00:53:48,267
Yeah, that's right.

1039
00:53:48,351 --> 00:53:49,936
Whose home was it?

1040
00:53:50,019 --> 00:53:51,145
X's home.

1041
00:53:51,228 --> 00:53:52,563
You went to X's home?

1042
00:53:52,647 --> 00:53:53,648
Really?

1043
00:53:54,231 --> 00:53:56,776
I'm not sure he should share that
when she's right there.

1044
00:53:56,859 --> 00:53:58,819
I might not like him sharing that.

1045
00:53:58,903 --> 00:53:59,987
Definitely.

1046
00:54:00,071 --> 00:54:00,905
True.

1047
00:54:00,988 --> 00:54:02,365
Her house?

1048
00:54:02,698 --> 00:54:04,700
Okay, I have a grown-up question.

1049
00:54:04,867 --> 00:54:06,786
Does that mean you were already
physically intimate?

1050
00:54:06,869 --> 00:54:07,912
No.

1051
00:54:07,995 --> 00:54:09,121
No?

1052
00:54:09,205 --> 00:54:12,583
So you were just sleeping in the same
bed like this?

1053
00:54:12,667 --> 00:54:13,918
Recreate it.

1054
00:54:14,961 --> 00:54:17,421
Dai-chan, let us borrow you.

1055
00:54:19,215 --> 00:54:21,217
Okay, I'll be X.

1056
00:54:21,467 --> 00:54:24,011
Come over here.

1057
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:27,098
I was like this. No, you weren't
like that.

1058
00:54:27,181 --> 00:54:29,976
We weren't that close.

1059
00:54:30,393 --> 00:54:31,477
No?

1060
00:54:31,560 --> 00:54:33,187
Because I was super nervous.

1061
00:54:33,270 --> 00:54:34,772
It's before they were officially dating.

1062
00:54:34,855 --> 00:54:35,982
A little further.

1063
00:54:36,065 --> 00:54:37,149
That much?

1064
00:54:37,233 --> 00:54:38,567
It's their first night.

1065
00:54:38,651 --> 00:54:40,152
That's so much detail.

1066
00:54:40,903 --> 00:54:42,363
"Can I say one thing?"

1067
00:54:43,280 --> 00:54:44,949
I asked her.

1068
00:54:46,534 --> 00:54:50,121
Then I asked,
"Would you be my girlfriend?"

1069
00:54:50,329 --> 00:54:51,539
That's really good.

1070
00:54:51,622 --> 00:54:52,957
Crazy.

1071
00:54:53,124 --> 00:54:55,167
And she told you it was okay after that?

1072
00:54:55,251 --> 00:54:57,628
More like, "Sure, that's fine, I guess."

1073
00:54:57,712 --> 00:55:01,007
Maybe not exactly like that,
but not too far off.

1074
00:55:01,090 --> 00:55:03,217
That was a good one.

1075
00:55:03,300 --> 00:55:04,135
So like…

1076
00:55:04,218 --> 00:55:05,094
How wonderful.

1077
00:55:05,177 --> 00:55:07,638
When I asked her to be my girlfriend,

1078
00:55:07,722 --> 00:55:10,808
it was the most nervous I'd ever been
in my life.

1079
00:55:11,726 --> 00:55:13,811
Were you planning to ask her that day
all along?

1080
00:55:13,894 --> 00:55:17,857
Yeah, because we were like this all day.

1081
00:55:18,482 --> 00:55:20,151
Okay, who goes next?

1082
00:55:20,234 --> 00:55:21,277
You can just call on someone.

1083
00:55:21,360 --> 00:55:22,278
Yeah?

1084
00:55:22,361 --> 00:55:24,071
Then

1085
00:55:25,531 --> 00:55:28,451
what did you not like

1086
00:55:28,534 --> 00:55:30,036
about X?

1087
00:55:30,578 --> 00:55:32,288
Good question.

1088
00:55:32,371 --> 00:55:33,497
That's a good question to ask.

1089
00:55:33,581 --> 00:55:34,498
It's usually the opposite.

1090
00:55:34,957 --> 00:55:36,292
I have so many.

1091
00:55:36,375 --> 00:55:38,127
You do?

1092
00:55:38,210 --> 00:55:39,837
You have so many?

1093
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:40,963
Please share then.

1094
00:55:41,047 --> 00:55:42,798
I have so many.

1095
00:55:42,882 --> 00:55:44,884
Honestly,

1096
00:55:45,259 --> 00:55:46,802
there were only things I didn't like.

1097
00:55:49,138 --> 00:55:52,141
Saying that in front of him must mean
it was pretty bad.

1098
00:55:52,224 --> 00:55:53,059
For real?

1099
00:55:54,518 --> 00:55:55,770
At the time,

1100
00:55:55,936 --> 00:55:59,815
he was so sweet before we started dating.

1101
00:55:59,899 --> 00:56:01,901
Or I mean,

1102
00:56:01,984 --> 00:56:05,029
he was really fun and funny.

1103
00:56:05,112 --> 00:56:08,407
But when we started dating,

1104
00:56:09,283 --> 00:56:11,494
it just became painful.

1105
00:56:12,661 --> 00:56:13,829
Like he was boring?

1106
00:56:13,913 --> 00:56:14,789
It was painful.

1107
00:56:14,872 --> 00:56:19,335
I mean, I'm sure we had some
fun times, too,

1108
00:56:21,170 --> 00:56:25,591
but for some reason, all I can remember
are the painful ones.

1109
00:56:32,306 --> 00:56:34,266
Misato-chan, let's go to the lounge.

1110
00:56:34,350 --> 00:56:36,602
Me? Okay.

1111
00:56:36,977 --> 00:56:38,187
Talk about anything interesting?

1112
00:56:38,687 --> 00:56:39,897
I'm all ears.

1113
00:56:39,980 --> 00:56:41,607
Any stories about your past with X?

1114
00:56:41,690 --> 00:56:43,984
We lived at the same station.

1115
00:56:44,068 --> 00:56:47,446
North side and south side
in our early 20s.

1116
00:56:47,863 --> 00:56:49,323
I get a phone call,

1117
00:56:49,657 --> 00:56:51,117
and I answer it.

1118
00:56:51,408 --> 00:56:53,828
He just says "Magazine and beer,"
and hangs up.

1119
00:56:55,246 --> 00:56:57,456
Yikes, that's scary.

1120
00:56:58,374 --> 00:57:00,668
My goodness.

1121
00:57:03,337 --> 00:57:07,383
So I go buy them and ride my bike
over to his place, right?

1122
00:57:07,466 --> 00:57:09,593
I ring the doorbell.

1123
00:57:09,677 --> 00:57:12,471
You figure we'd hang out
after I bought them for him.

1124
00:57:12,555 --> 00:57:14,348
Like a home date.

1125
00:57:14,932 --> 00:57:18,477
So I go, he opens the door a crack
and swipes them out of my hand.

1126
00:57:19,353 --> 00:57:20,563
Then shuts the door.

1127
00:57:20,646 --> 00:57:22,356
I'm just dumbfounded.

1128
00:57:22,439 --> 00:57:24,984
People do this?

1129
00:57:25,234 --> 00:57:28,362
There's no way he would still do that.
I'm sure he changed in his late 20s.

1130
00:57:28,445 --> 00:57:29,822
I'm not so sure about that.

1131
00:57:29,905 --> 00:57:31,282
That's crazy scary.

1132
00:57:31,782 --> 00:57:35,077
Yeah.

1133
00:57:47,965 --> 00:57:52,636
All these memories started flooding in.

1134
00:57:55,306 --> 00:57:58,601
People would ask me questions,

1135
00:57:59,727 --> 00:58:01,228
and I'd just answer them.

1136
00:58:01,312 --> 00:58:03,772
And that made me remember so much.

1137
00:58:04,940 --> 00:58:06,650
Bad memories.

1138
00:58:07,067 --> 00:58:08,819
It was hard,

1139
00:58:10,112 --> 00:58:13,115
and I never want to feel
like that ever again.

1140
00:58:17,536 --> 00:58:21,415
It's really tough.

1141
00:58:36,263 --> 00:58:38,140
Have you ever fought with your X?

1142
00:58:38,224 --> 00:58:39,058
No.

1143
00:58:39,350 --> 00:58:40,976
No?

1144
00:58:41,060 --> 00:58:43,103
Then, what was the reason for breaking up?

1145
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:45,773
We were wondering about that, too.

1146
00:58:47,650 --> 00:58:51,695
I don't know the reason why we broke up.

1147
00:58:53,113 --> 00:58:56,951
We had a talk where she told me
this was what she wanted to do.

1148
00:58:57,117 --> 00:59:00,329
And it basically ended because I agreed
to give her what she wanted.

1149
00:59:00,412 --> 00:59:03,415
I don't know what she disliked
about our relationship.

1150
00:59:03,749 --> 00:59:07,503
So I would keep asking myself
what it could've been.

1151
00:59:07,586 --> 00:59:08,629
Right.

1152
00:59:09,588 --> 00:59:11,715
The reason we broke up

1153
00:59:12,216 --> 00:59:15,511
was that she suggested it would be better
if we went back to being friends.

1154
00:59:15,594 --> 00:59:16,845
He mentions that often.

1155
00:59:16,929 --> 00:59:18,764
It was her suggestion.

1156
00:59:19,390 --> 00:59:21,809
And when I agreed to it, that was it.

1157
00:59:22,476 --> 00:59:24,645
When we broke up,

1158
00:59:24,728 --> 00:59:27,314
I know we talked a few times
around that time,

1159
00:59:28,816 --> 00:59:30,693
but you know how you just feel it?

1160
00:59:31,402 --> 00:59:33,862
Like you wanted to express something.

1161
00:59:33,946 --> 00:59:36,490
That something felt off.

1162
00:59:39,368 --> 00:59:40,452
Right.

1163
00:59:42,329 --> 00:59:43,622
So

1164
00:59:43,706 --> 00:59:48,460
I often reflect on how
I could've done better

1165
00:59:49,586 --> 00:59:52,756
through my actions and communication.

1166
01:00:04,393 --> 01:00:07,438
To be honest,

1167
01:00:07,688 --> 01:00:09,732
the biggest thing was

1168
01:00:10,816 --> 01:00:12,860
physical intimacy.

1169
01:00:17,364 --> 01:00:18,657
Well,

1170
01:00:21,285 --> 01:00:23,871
he didn't seem to have much
of a sex drive.

1171
01:00:27,416 --> 01:00:31,128
I came to this hocance
hoping to learn why.

1172
01:00:31,211 --> 01:00:32,212
You know?

1173
01:00:32,796 --> 01:00:35,507
Wait, so Daichi doesn't know?

1174
01:00:35,758 --> 01:00:37,426
He clearly doesn't.
